{"title":"Coterminal angles","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Angles are said to be coterminal if their angle measures differ by a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645991b0a28774e0aa8f5b88ea3aa53318e848ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ} = 2\\pi \\, \\mathrm{rad}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />. Coterminal angles are equivalent in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane\" title=\"Plane\">plane</a> and share the same values of all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometry\" title=\"Trigonometry\">trigonometric functions</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Coterminal_angles&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 205/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.424      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.424      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22601:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081728 and revision id 172579. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}